{
 "_readme": [
  "The one place for what is on each screen and where. Edit it, then run python tools/build_map.py (or python tools/layout.py to check).",
  "tabs: the header tabs, in order. Set \"visible\": false to hide one.",
  "screens.<tab>.cols: the columns, each a list of widget ids from top to bottom. Move an id to move the widget. Add its id to \"hidden\" to hide it.",
  "widgets.<id>: how a widget is wrapped. dom_id = the element id other code looks for; variant = an extra card class (night = the dark card); tag = \"aside\"; plain = no entrance animation; fixed_i = fixed stagger position; raw = the widget draws its own card. screens.<name>.flat = cards side by side with no column wrappers.",
  "A widget is written once with UI.widget(\"<id>\", ctx => html) in tools/site_assets/app/widgets-*.js. Colours and sizes come from theme.json, never from here."
 ],
